From 4618056f0800ba9d5eca0ace65ebea1d2948f321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rico Rojas <rickrojas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 17:34:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hotkey): hybrid activation mode, tap to latch or hold to
 talk

Add a third dictation activation mode, "hybrid", alongside tap and push.
A press starts the push state machine as before; a release under 400 ms
latches the recording on until the next press, a longer hold stops on
release. A press while a latched recording runs is the stop tap. Forced
releases (listener reset, safety timeout) never latch.

The decisions live in src/helpers/activationMode.js as pure functions
(resolveDictationPress / resolveDictationRelease) with unit tests; the
five key-release sites (Globe, right modifier, mouse button, macOS
compound, Windows/Linux native) call them and share
windowManager.applyDictationRelease. The hotkey layer still registers
hybrid as push, so it is available exactly where Hold is.

Settings and onboarding show a three-way Tap / Hold / Both selector; the
env var, store, and IPC types accept "hybrid". Locale keys common.hybrid
and onboarding.activation.hybridDescription added to every language in
English.

Closes openwhispr#1.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015uYKeUK2xoKRQMj5gCikCq
